  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "gleich",
      "regel": [
        "Many short words come in two forms: with a written accent and without one. **The accent changes the word**: *tu* = your, *tú* = you.",
        "Question words carry an accent, also in the middle of a sentence: *¿qué?*, *¿dónde?*, *no sé qué hacer*.",
        "The letter **h** is silent, so *a* and *ha*, *hola* and *ola* sound the same. Ask what kind of word you need."
      ],
      "regelTr": {},
      "title": "Sounds the same, spelt differently",
      "lead": "You can't hear the difference, or hardly at all. In writing you see it at once.",
      "pairs": [
        {
          "id": "tu-tu",
          "level": "A1",
          "a": {
            "w": "tu",
            "pos": "possessive: your",
            "ex": "¿Es <b>tu</b> bolso?"
          },
          "b": {
            "w": "tú",
            "pos": "pronoun: you",
            "ex": "<b>Tú</b> hablas muy bien."
          },
          "why": "tú with an accent is the person: you. tu without one means your: tu casa.",
          "tr": {},
          "check": {
            "gap": "¿Cómo se llama ___ hermano?",
            "answer": "a"
          },
          "variety": "es-ES"
        },
